  "Channel 2 popularity proxy is the DEGRADED v2-score order within bucket (Deezer rank not stored on disk).",
  "Pool buckets: artist map 112/590 direct, via_artist fallback 478/590, unknown 0/590.",
  "O-bucket tracks are excluded from genre-filtered channel 1 (treated as unknown-genre per spec b.5); reachable via channels 2-4 and merge back-fill.",
  "NDCG@10 QUIRK (evaluate.py ndcg_at_k): the ideal DCG is computed from the relevant items IN THE TOP 10 only, not from all 99 held-out likes, so NDCG@10 measures within-top-10 ordering, not standard NDCG. All methods use the same function, so relative comparisons hold; absolute values are not comparable to standard NDCG.",
  "Zero-score tail: items outside every channel score 0.0 (~180/311); they are tie-broken by acoustic cosine to the seed (a real signal), not title order, so mean-rank legs are measurements rather than tie-break artifacts. P@10/NDCG@10 are unaffected (top 10 all score > 0).",
  "Channel-4 conflict: contribution rate 8/20 (40%) is below the d.2.3 50% cut line, but removing channel 4 costs 0.10 P@10 (ablation minus_channel4), so per the b.4 ablation rule it is NOT redundant. Channel 4 is KEPT; the conflict is flagged for the coordinator.",
  "Ablation NDCG note: removing channel 1 improves NDCG@10 (0.829 -> 0.948) while P@10 is unchanged (0.60); the d.2.3 ablation rule is stated on P@10 only, so no channel is cut on that rule, but channel 1 hurts within-top-10 ordering.",
  "Spec d.2.1 \">=17 additional held-out likes\" is wrong: +0.05 P@10 is +0.5 held-out likes in a top 10.",
  "Spec d.2.2 neg-rank leg is unsatisfiable vs v2 (292.9+20 > 311); evaluated vs best-P@10 baseline v6-global (178.2).",
  "Final-score rescale implemented as linear max->2.0; the spec-quoted formula is self-contradictory (maps max to ~0.55)."
